            "yMin": -10,
            "yMax": 12
          },
          "solutionReview": {
            "headline": "Two horizontal inequalities create a horizontal strip.",
            "reasoning": [
              "The boundary y={{lower}} is solid and shades above.",
              "The boundary y={{upper}} is solid and shades below.",
              "The common solution is the strip between the two boundaries, including both lines."
            ],
            "answerSummary": "Shade {{lower}}≤y≤{{upper}}."
          },
          "attemptFeedback": [
            "Graph each horizontal boundary separately, then keep only the region satisfying both."
          ],
          "supportHints": [
            "For y≥constant shade above; for y≤constant shade below."
